+  * Update cipher-related man page text (Steffan Karger, db6cdf9)
+  * make t_client robust against sudoers misconfiguration (Gert Doering, 0bd4ef0)
+  * Automatically cache expected IPs for t_client.sh on the first run (Samuli Seppänen, beca355)
+  * Fix t_client runs on OpenSolaris (Gert Doering, c32f58c)
+  * Incorporate the Debian typo fixes where appropriate and make show_opt default message clearer (Arne Schwabe, 1f12d8d)
+  * t_client.sh: Improve detection if the OpenVPN process did start during tests (David Sommerseth, 3347d51)
+  * t_client.sh: Add support for Kerberos/ksu (David Sommerseth, f1b66b2)
+  * skip t_lpback.sh and t_cltsrv.sh if openvpn configured --disable-crypto (Ilya Shipitsin, 8e13e38)
+  * t_client.sh: Make OpenVPN write PID file to avoid various sudo issues (David Sommerseth, 057b70f)
+  * cleanup: remove code duplication in msg_test() (Steffan Karger, 59114b9)
+  * Make gnu89 support explicit (Steffan Karger, 130c27b)
+  * Do not abort t_client run if OpenVPN instance does not start. (Gert Doering, 0043ddb)
+  * Use AES ciphers in our sample configuration files and add a few modern 2.4 examples (Arne Schwabe, 0b47074)
+  * Fix unittests for out-of-source builds (Steffan Karger, 57294aa)
+
