+openvpn (2.3.15-debian0) stable; urgency=high
+
+  * Prepare v2.3.15 release (David Sommerseth, 3902e56a)
+  * Don't assert out on receiving too-large control packets (CVE-2017-7478) (Steffan Karger, feb35ee5)
+  * Drop packets instead of assert out if packet id rolls over (CVE-2017-7479) (Steffan Karger, b727643c)
+  * Introduce and use secure_memzero() to erase secrets (Steffan Karger, e80c659d)
+  * Document that OpenVPN 2.3 does not check the CRL signature (Steffan Karger, 51d936d0)
+  * cleanup: merge packet_id_alloc_outgoing() into packet_id_write() (Steffan Karger, 5d747770)
+  * Add missing includes in error.h (Steffan Karger, 895abd4b)
+  * Make --cipher/--auth none more explicit on the risks (David Sommerseth, 32b5cb60)
+  * Document --proto udp6, tcp6, etc. (Gert Doering, 69c4e064)
+  * git: Merge .gitignore files into a single file (David Sommerseth, 61da0031)
+  * Fix implicit declarations when HAVE_OPENSSL_ENGINE is unset (Julien Muchembled, ab1302d4)
+  * docs: Further improve --reneg-bytes and SWEET32 information (David Sommerseth, 49e6ce5b)
+  * Update copyrights (David Sommerseth, 782c9533)
+  * dev-tools: Added script for updating copyright years in files (David Sommerseth, 9e2bbbc7)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Thu, 11 May 2017 11:00:00 +0000
+
+openvpn (2.3.14-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Preparing release of v2.3.14 (Gert Doering, 117dadc)
+  * Correctly state the default dhcp server address in man page (Selva Nair, a1b9e4c)
+  * Map restart signals from event loop to SIGTERM during exit-notification wait (Selva Nair, 4d397fc)
+  * When parsing '--setenv opt xx ..' make sure a third parameter is present (Selva Nair, 290cc3f)
+  * update year in copyright message (Christian Hesse, 64dc639)
+  * Clean up format_hex_ex() (Steffan Karger, 3843024)
+  * Document the --auth-token option (David Sommerseth, d5cb6b4)
+  * Support --block-outside-dns on multiple tunnels (Selva Nair, f65f852)
+  * Repair topology subnet on OpenBSD (Gert Doering, ceac73b)
+  * Repair topology subnet on FreeBSD 11 (Gert Doering, 446ef5b)
+  * Drop recursively routed packets (Lev Stipakov, 748974b)
+  * man: Improve the --keepalive section (David Sommerseth, 2877822)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Wed, 7 Dec 2016 12:10:00 +0000
+
+openvpn (2.3.13-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Preparing release of v2.3.13 (David Sommerseth, f44354e)
+  * Add a revoked cert to the sample keys (Steffan Karger, bac347d)
+  * Limit --reneg-bytes to 64MB when using small block ciphers (Steffan Karger, a91ddc9)
+  * Fix compilation in pedantic mode (Lev Stipakov, d72c383)
+  * Exclude peer-id from pulled options digest (Lev Stipakov, 8402203)
+  * Fix --multihome for IPv6 on 64bit BSD systems. (Gert Doering, f7aba87)
+  * add POSTINIT_CMD_suf to t_client.sh and sample config (Gert Doering, 7891c8c)
+  * t_client.sh: Add prepare/cleanup possibilties for each test case (David Sommerseth, 6ac1cf1)
+  * Update cipher-related man page text (Steffan Karger, db6cdf9)
+  * make t_client robust against sudoers misconfiguration (Gert Doering, 0bd4ef0)
+  * Automatically cache expected IPs for t_client.sh on the first run (Samuli Seppänen, beca355)
+  * Fix t_client runs on OpenSolaris (Gert Doering, c32f58c)
+  * Incorporate the Debian typo fixes where appropriate and make show_opt default message clearer (Arne Schwabe, 1f12d8d)
+  * t_client.sh: Improve detection if the OpenVPN process did start during tests (David Sommerseth, 3347d51)
+  * t_client.sh: Add support for Kerberos/ksu (David Sommerseth, f1b66b2)
+  * skip t_lpback.sh and t_cltsrv.sh if openvpn configured --disable-crypto (Ilya Shipitsin, 8e13e38)
+  * t_client.sh: Make OpenVPN write PID file to avoid various sudo issues (David Sommerseth, 057b70f)
+  * cleanup: remove code duplication in msg_test() (Steffan Karger, 59114b9)
+  * Make gnu89 support explicit (Steffan Karger, 130c27b)
+  * Do not abort t_client run if OpenVPN instance does not start. (Gert Doering, 0043ddb)
+  * Use AES ciphers in our sample configuration files and add a few modern 2.4 examples (Arne Schwabe, 0b47074)
+  * Fix unittests for out-of-source builds (Steffan Karger, 57294aa)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Thu, 3 Nov 2016 09:30:00 +0000
+
+openvpn (2.3.12-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
