+openvpn (2.4.3-debian0) stable; urgency=high
+
+  * Preparing for release v2.4.3 (ChangeLog, version.m4, Changes.rst) (Gert Doering, db34435)
+  * Fix remotely-triggerable ASSERT() on malformed IPv6 packet. (Gert Doering, ed28cde)
+  * Prevent two kinds of stack buffer OOB reads and a crash for invalid input data (Guido Vranken, 043fe32)
+  * Fix potential double-free in --x509-alt-username (CVE-2017-7521) (Steffan Karger, 0400840)
+  * Restrict --x509-alt-username extension types (Steffan Karger, b72472b)
+  * Fix remote-triggerable memory leaks (CVE-2017-7521) (Steffan Karger, 2341f71)
+  * mbedtls: require C-string compatible types for --x509-username-field (Steffan Karger, 20f1a47)
+  * mbedtls: fix --x509-track post-authentication remote DoS (CVE-2017-7522) (Steffan Karger, 67edada)
+  * auth-token with auth-nocache fix broke --disable-crypto builds (David Sommerseth, df5efe7)
+  * Ignore auth-nocache for auth-user-pass if auth-token is pushed (Antonio Quartulli, e4b0600)
+  * Fix potential 1-byte overread in TCP option parsing. (Gert Doering, 529de43)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of HMAC_CTX (Emmanuel Deloget, 2bf4aee)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of EVP_CIPHER_CTX (Emmanuel Deloget, a5ac1ec)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of EVP_MD_CTX (Emmanuel Deloget, 87a3923)
+  * Fix mbedtls fingerprint calculation (Steffan Karger, d7b7f93)
+  * Add a DSA test key/cert pair to sample-keys (Steffan Karger, d937bb7)
+  * OpenSSL: force meth->name as non-const when we free() it (Emmanuel Deloget, 57eaf99)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of DSA (Emmanuel Deloget, 6f5aa04)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of RSA (Emmanuel Deloget, dd1ae0e)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of EVP_PKEY (Emmanuel Deloget, cc7c912)
+  * OpenSSL: don't use direct access to the internal of X509 (Emmanuel Deloget, e78934a)
+  * Fix edge case with clients failing to set up cipher on empty PUSH_REPLY. (Gert Doering, e82f700)
+  * copyright: Update GPLv2 license texts (David Sommerseth, b11f646)
+  * Fix a null-pointer dereference in establish_http_proxy_passthru() (Guido Vranken, bf547b8)
+  * openssl: fix overflow check for long --tls-cipher option (Steffan Karger, b52c1ff)
+  * Skip tls-crypt unit tests if required crypto mode not supported (Steffan Karger, 84372cb)
+  * Ensure option array p[] is always NULL-terminated (Guido Vranken, 110f1e1)
+  * Missing include for socket-flags TCP_NODELAY on OpenBSD (Jérémie Courrèges-Anglas, fc6b630)
+  * Fix an unaligned access on OpenBSD/sparc64 (Jérémie Courrèges-Anglas, 29ba477)
+  * Fix memory leak in add_option() for option 'connection' (Guido Vranken, 42fc73b)
+  * Fix 2 memory leaks in proxy authentication routine (Guido Vranken, ec204e1)
+  * refactor my_strupr (Guido Vranken, 69f00d8)
+  * Remove erroneous limitation on max number of args for --plugin (Gert Doering, a4d200a)
+  * Fix gateway detection with OpenBSD routing domains (Steven McDonald, 212e24d)
+  * Avoid a 1 byte overcopy in x509_get_subject (ssl_verify_openssl.c) (Steffan Karger, a91c54d)
+  * Fix NCP behaviour on TLS reconnect. (Gert Doering, 13c05ca)
+  * crypto: Enable SHA256 fingerprint checking in --verify-hash (David Sommerseth, 5d54377)
+  * Make openvpn-plugin.h self-contained again. (Matthias Andree, 37b3409)
+  * Log the negotiated (NCP) cipher (Steffan Karger, 4ae06ef)
+  * Pass correct buffer size to GetModuleFileNameW() (Selva Nair, 9092397)
