+openvpn (2.4.7-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * preparing release v2.4.7 (ChangeLog, version.m4, Changes.rst) (Gert Doering, 2b8aec62)
+  * White-list pull-filter and script-security in interactive service (Selva Nair, b8190ecb)
+  * Detect TAP interfaces with root-enumerated hardware ID (Simon Rozman, eef040cc)
+  * Fix error message when using RHEL init script (Richard van den Berg via Openvpn-devel, d18fa4aa)
+  * Add 'printing of port number' to mroute_addr_print_ex() for v4-mapped v6. (Gert Doering, c2f70587)
+  * Fallback to password authentication when auth-token fails (Arne Schwabe, 004f13b6)
+  * Remove extra token after #endif (Lev Stipakov, ca962f38)
+  * Add message explaining early TLS client hello failure (Arne Schwabe, dd029af6)
+  * ifconfig-ipv6(-push): allow using hostnames (Antonio Quartulli, 1e3672c9)
+  * buffer_list_aggregate_separator(): simplify code (Steffan Karger, be47e429)
+  * buffer_list: add functions documentation (Antonio Quartulli, 61ef9057)
+  * Use right function to set TLS1.3 restrictions in show-tls (Arne Schwabe, 33253cf1)
+  * Add better support for showing TLS 1.3 ciphersuites in --show-tls (Arne Schwabe, e8467c86)
+  * options.c: fix broken unary minus usage (Lev Stipakov, 62eb234c)
+  * Add support for tls-ciphersuites for TLS 1.3 (Arne Schwabe, 9de7fe0a)
+  * interactive.c: fix usage of potentially uninitialized variable (Lev Stipakov, 773c0863)
+  * man: correct a --redirection-gateway option flag (Samy Mahmoudi, d6637316)
+  * Don't print OCC warnings about 'key-method', 'keydir' and 'tls-auth' (Steffan Karger, 266178b7)
+  * Fix combination of --dev tap and --topology subnet across multiple platforms. (Gert Doering, 6c13e24e)
+  * init.c: refine functions names and description (Lev Stipakov, 6f8fb6fe)
+  * Pass the hash without the DigestInfo header to NCryptSignHash() (Selva Nair, 163fa9c1)
+  * Fix --disable-crypto build (Steffan Karger, ee80ce3d)
+  * Enable dhcp on tap adapter using interactive service (Selva Nair, 78d4f0ad)
+  * travis: add OpenSSL 1.1 Windows build (Steffan Karger, b8d8e492)
+  * Move get system directory to a separate function (Selva Nair, f0516a80)
+  * Add OpenSSL compat definition for RSA_meth_set_sign (Arne Schwabe, c75e9376)
+  * Refactor NCP-negotiable options handling (Lev Stipakov, d2ff5164)
+  * Properly free tuntap struct on android when emulating persist-tun (Arne Schwabe, 21a307dd)
+  * systemd: extend CapabilityBoundingSet for auth_pam (Christian Ehrhardt, 7cc372c7)
+  * Fix memory leak after sighup (Steffan Karger, 8fcfe1d4)
+  * mbedtls: print warning if random personalisation fails (Steffan Karger, 0c6323cd)
+  * Clarify and expand management interface documentation (Jonathan K. Bullard, 9b71d1d2)
+  * Fix subnet topology on NetBSD (2.4). (Adam Ciarciński, de4c7767)
+  * Bump version of openvpn plugin argument structs to 5 (Selva Nair, d8496285)
+  * plugin: Export base64 encode and decode functions (David Sommerseth, 6c261167)
+  * Resolves small IV_GUI_VER typo in the documentation. (James Bekkema, 4c38e382)
+  * Correct the declaration of handle in 'struct openvpn_plugin_args_open_return' (Selva Nair, 359e66bc)
+  * Minor reliability layer documentation fixes (Gert van Dijk, 52e6de50)
+  * Add %d, %u and %lu tests to test_argv unit tests. (Gert Doering, 6b27704d)
+  * add support for %lu in argv_printf and prevent ASSERT (Antonio Quartulli, 61dcf151)
+  * Add Interactive Service developer documentation (Simon Rozman, 9e1800da)
+  * Replace M_DEBUG with D_LOW as the former is too verbose (Selva Nair, 935d1706)
+  * man: add security considerations to --compress section (Steffan Karger, 6795a5f3)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Tue, 19 Feb 2019 13:20:00 +0000
+
