+openvpn (2.4_rc1-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Preparing OpenVPN v2.4_rc1 release (David Sommerseth, e739d7f)
+  * Refuse to daemonize when running from systemd (Christian Hesse, 7660bba)
+  * Use systemd service manager notification (Christian Hesse, c593189)
+  * Mention that OpenVPN 2.4 requires Windows Vista or higher (Samuli Seppänen, 1c587a1)
+  * reload CRL only if file was modified (Antonio Quartulli, ce91c18)
+  * Do not restart dns client service as a part of --register-dns processing (Selva Nair, fb56058)
+  * Force 'def1' method when --redirect-gateway is done through service (Selva Nair, 788e5e4)
+  * When parsing '--setenv opt xx ..' make sure a third parameter is present (Selva Nair, 9977953)
+  * Introduce and use secure_memzero() to erase secrets (Steffan Karger, 009521a)
+  * Map restart signals from event loop to SIGTERM during exit-notification wait (Selva Nair, f25a021)
+  * Fix windows path in Changes.rst (Gert Doering, 6c6456f)
+  * update year in copyright message (Christian Hesse, 7f7d6b2)
+  * Clean up format_hex_ex() (Steffan Karger, 2940401)
+  * Unconditionally enable TLS_AGGREGATE_ACK (Steffan Karger, 7182578)
+  * tls_process: don't set variable that's never read (Steffan Karger, 06c5446)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Fri, 2 Dec 2016 07:30:00 +0000
+
+openvpn (2.4_beta2-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Preparing OpenVPN v2.4_beta2 release (David Sommerseth, 9bc2be7)
+  * Set IPv6 DNS servers using interactive service (Selva Nair, c098016)
+  * Refactor data channel key generation API (Steffan Karger, e2ffdb7)
+  * Poor man's NCP for non-NCP peers (Steffan Karger, 6e5ad2f)
+  * Document the --auth-token option (David Sommerseth, f8a367f)
+  * generate_key_expansion: make assumption explicit, use C99 features (Steffan Karger, 48d4141)
+  * Change cmocka remote to use https in stead of git protocol (Steffan Karger, da94114)
+  * --tls-crypt fixes (Steffan Karger, 418d2d9)
+  * Handle DNS6 option on Android (Arne Schwabe, 39b7d4d)
+  * Handle --dhcp-option DNS6 on Windows using netsh (Selva Nair, 786e06a)
+  * Stub implementation of "--dhcp-option DNS6 <v6addr>" (Gert Doering, 94bfc25)
+  * Do not set ipv6 address if '--ip-win32 manual' is used (Selva Nair, d6ad8ca)
+  * Remove remaining traces of compat-stdbool.h (Gert Doering, e5fc56a)
+  * Fix various compiler warnings (Arne Schwabe, 3212d0c)
+  * Remove compat-stdbool.h. (Arne Schwabe, 35be7e0)
+  * Fix warning that RAND_bytes is undeclared (Arne Schwabe, 6ede22c)
+  * multi_process_float: revert part of c14c4a9e (Steffan Karger, c593885)
+  * Document that tls-crypt also supports inline (Arne Schwabe, 8025a62)
+  * Changes.rst: Fixing wrong formatting (David Sommerseth, 237fd7f)
+
+ -- Samuli Seppänen <samuli@openvpn.net>  Fri, 25 Nov 2016 07:30:00 +0000
+
+openvpn (2.4_alpha2-debian0) stable; urgency=medium
+
+  * Preparing for release v2.4_alpha2 (ChangeLog, version.m4) (Gert Doering, d600b2c)
+  * Fix use-after-free bug in prepare_push_reply() (Steffan Karger, 83fdae3)
+  * Update .mailmap to unify and clean up odd names and e-mail addresses (David Sommerseth, a47d349)
+  * Preparing for release v2.4_alpha1 (ChangeLog, version.m4) (Gert Doering, a6479b4)
+  * Windows: do_ifconfig() after open_tun() (Heiko Hund, 5334952)
+  * Remove tun-ipv6 Option. Instead assume that IPv6 is always supported. (Arne Schwabe, 86e2fa5)
+  * Move memcmp_constant_time() to crypto.h (David Sommerseth, b891e57)
+  * Check --ncp-ciphers list on startup (Steffan Karger, dc4fa3c)
+  * Change the hold command to communicate the time that OpenVPN would wait to the UI. (Arne Schwabe, 396d30c)
+  * Use separate list for per-client push options (Lev Stipakov, 88c4b9d)
+  * systemd: Do not mask usernames when querying for it via systemd-ask-password (David Sommerseth, 8ba3e25)
+  * Re-implement the systemd support using the new query user API (David Sommerseth, 3280d8c)
+  * Rework the user input interface to make it more modular (David Sommerseth, 430ce8b)
+  * Enable TCP non-linear packet ID (Arne Schwabe, 55755e6)
+  * Enable -D_XPG4_2 for compilation on Solaris (Gert Doering, 4e2038e)
+  * Revert "Enable -D_SVR4_2 for compilation on Solaris" (Gert Doering, e25d03a)
+  * Fix duplicate PUSH_REPLY options (Steffan Karger, 974ec19)
+  * Exclude peer-id from pulled options digest (Lev Stipakov, 3cf51f6)
+  * Enable -D_SVR4_2 for compilation on Solaris (Gert Doering, 6eaa70e)
+  * Fix --multihome for IPv6 on 64bit BSD systems. (Gert Doering, 3fb246e)
+  * add POSTINIT_CMD_suf to t_client.sh and sample config (Gert Doering, bae1ad7)
+  * Update cipher-related man page text (Steffan Karger, 5a1daf5)
+  * make t_client robust against sudoers misconfiguration (Gert Doering, 8ca29af)
+  * Automatically cache expected IPs for t_client.sh on the first run (Samuli Seppänen, df0b00c)
+  * Make sure options->ciphername and options->authname are always defined (Steffan Karger, 348c416)
+  * enable "--disable-crypto" build configuration for travis (Ilya Shipitsin, 0c72e29)
+  * Fix t_client runs on OpenSolaris (Gert Doering, 38f98fd)
+  * Fix win32 building with C99 mode (Gert Doering, 6cd7e08)
+  * Incorporate the Debian typo fixes where appropriate and make show_opt default message clearer (Arne Schwabe, c42fcbf)
+  * Support for disabled peer-id (Lev Stipakov, e8e1377)
+  * Prefer RECVDSTADDR to PKTINFO for IPv4 in OS X since it actually works (unlike PKTINFO) (Arne Schwabe, e7303ac)
+  * Add SHA256 fingerprint support (Steffan Karger, af1e4d2)
+  * Fix ENABLE_CRYPTO_OPENSSL set to YES even with --disable-crypto set (Arne Schwabe, d13a40a)
+  * t_client.sh: Improve detection if the OpenVPN process did start during tests (David Sommerseth, 3712322)
+  * t_client.sh: Add support for Kerberos/ksu (David Sommerseth, 6b25b99)
+  * Show compile-time variant for --multihome in --version output. (Gert Doering, d7c15ff)
+  * Fix IP_PKTINFO related compilation failure on NetBSD 7.0 (Gert Doering, 7efa60d)
+  * skip t_lpback.sh and t_cltsrv.sh if openvpn configured --disable-crypto (Ilya Shipitsin, a85ba0e)
+  * t_client.sh: Make OpenVPN write PID file to avoid various sudo issues (David Sommerseth, e0926eb)
+  * initial travis-ci support (Ilya Shipitsin, 3689912)
+  * cleanup: remove code duplication in msg_test() (Steffan Karger, d7ce876)
+  * Do not abort t_client run if OpenVPN instance does not start. (Gert Doering, a7b02f7)
+  * Drop gnu89/c89 support, switch to c99 (Steffan Karger, 058f0ef)
+  * Fix --mssfix when using NCP (Steffan Karger, cbc3c5a)
+  * Fix client connection instant timeout (David Sommerseth, 4db0629)
+  * Bind to local socket before dropping privileges (James Yonan, b3e9758)
+  * Use AES ciphers in our sample configuration files and add a few modern 2.4 examples (Arne Schwabe, bde1b90)
+  * Fix unittests for out-of-source builds (Steffan Karger, ee4f37c)
+  * Revert "Drop recursively routed packets" (David Sommerseth, 8cba9ff)
+  * Fix problems with NCP and --inetd. (Gert Doering, d90249f)
+  * Drop recursively routed packets (Lev Stipakov, e9d64bc)
+  * Discourage using 64-bit block ciphers (Steffan Karger, c94b3ff)
+  * Avoid format specifier %zu for Windows compatibility (Selva Nair, d1bd37f)
+  * Fix '--cipher none --cipher' crash (Steffan Karger, dea8917)
+  * Allow ncp-disable and ncp-ciphers to be specified in ccd files (Steffan Karger, 834f602)
+  * Add server-side support for cipher negotiation (Steffan Karger, a17aa98)
+  * Add options to restrict cipher negotiation (Steffan Karger, d728ebe)
+  * Update android documentation to match source code (Arne Schwabe, 49817bf)
+  * Add client-side support for cipher negotiation (Steffan Karger, 9789436)
+  * Deprecate the automatic part of openvpnserv.exe in favor of openvpnserv2.exe (Samuli Seppänen, 6dd307c)
+  * Promptly close the netcmd_semaphore handle after use (Selva Nair, 6aa4c90)
+  * Exponentially back off on repeated connect retries (Selva Nair, 5d429ef)
+  * Remove NOP function and callers (David Sommerseth, 365506d)
+  * Remove http-proxy-retry and socks-proxy-retry. (Arne Schwabe, 2011b83)
+  * Return process id of openvpn from interactive service to client (Selva Nair, e4c9bbe)
+  * Fix management-external-cert option parsing error (Selva Nair, d023fb6)
+  * Clarify which Windows versions require which TUN/TAP driver (Samuli Seppänen, 3f0edd8)
+  * Use an up-to-date easy-rsa URL on the man-page (Samuli Seppänen, d16ea8b)
+  * Mention tap-windows6 in INSTALL file (Samuli Seppänen, ac341e6)
+  * Add documentation for http-proxy-user-pass option (Arne Schwabe, ec0c1dc)
+  * Added directive to specify HTTP proxy credentials in config. (James Yonan, c9a35a2)
+  * mbedtls: don't set debug threshold if compiled without MBEDTLS_DEBUG_C (Steffan Karger, b63f986)
+  * Remove http-proxy-timeout, socks timeout and set default of server-poll-timeout to 120s (Arne Schwabe, f2134b7)
+  * Complete push-peer-info documentation and allow IV_PLAT_VER for other platforms than Windows if the client UI supplies it. (Arne Schwabe, 960524a)
+  * Change --enable-pedantic to use -std=c99 and not -ansi (C90). (Gert Doering, d16072c)
+  * Upgrade bundled compat-lz4 to upstream release r131. (Gert Doering, 46e4b66)
